    {
      "id": "R007",
      "decision": "d-pending-owner-cuda-ode-shared-projection-20261125",
      "change": "The FMI3 projection kernel and its typed-function and scalar-kernel templates render, behind a device flag, a build in which every function is a static device function, the instance and its arena live in caller storage, and typed calls pass named arrays instead of compound literals; the host components render as before. The kernel also renders the parameter-binding runs, the initialization on the instance coordinates with its row isolators and partial forward Jacobian, the delays held at their source during initialization and the projection onto the retained state manifold, each from the plans issued by rumoca-ir-solve. On a device, runs of whole programs and switch dispatchers are split into out-of-line groups of bounded size. The cuda-ode target renders one model instance per lane through that kernel (refresh, initialization, state manifold, step-only builds) from a per-lane execution view of the Solve model. No renderer derives a plan.",
